From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] igmp: keep a static group's refresh running when one of its
 ports stops

A static group's refresh timer (l2_static_grp_tmr, one per static group of
a VLAN) renews the static membership of every port in the group's port
tree every query interval, below the group membership time. When any one
of those ports stopped (link down, snooping off, a version change),
mcgrp_stop_phy_port() deleted that timer, and only a static port's next
link-up (mcgrp_add_l2_staticGroup() from the replay) started it again.
Meanwhile the other ports' static memberships aged out one group
membership time after their last refresh, with a member delete sent for
each, and stayed out. On a switch whose uplink was a static member of a
VLAN's groups beside a test port that flapped, the uplink's memberships
went 260 s after the last refresh, at the second, each time the test port
had lost link in between, and for good after its last link-down.

The timer is left running. mcgrp_refresh_l2_static_group() now skips a
port that is not up, as mcgrp_update_l2_static_group() and
mcgrp_refresh_static_group() already do; without that the running refresh
would make a static membership for a port with no link. The port's own
membership still comes back with its link-up replay.

That replay adds the port to the group's port tree again, though a
stopped port stays in it: avl_probe() returns the node already in the
tree, so mld_sg_porttree_addport() kept its new node and leaked it, once
per static group at every link-up of a static port. It is freed now.

The harness's static-member-link-down and mld-static-member-link-down
cases (two static ports, one loses link, 600 s, the link comes back) lose
the other port's static membership without this; static-member-reported
and mld-static-member-reported (a static port that also reports the group)
pass either way.
---
 port/l2mcd_mld_port.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 src/igmp.c            | 17 +++++------------
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/port/l2mcd_mld_port.c b/port/l2mcd_mld_port.c
index 48fdf13..fff66f8 100644
--- a/port/l2mcd_mld_port.c
+++ b/port/l2mcd_mld_port.c
@@ -2197,6 +2197,7 @@ MCGRP_STATIC_ENTRY * mcgrp_add_l2_staticGroup(MCGRP_CLASS * mcgrp,
 int mld_sg_porttree_addport(L2MCD_AVL_TREE *port_tree, uint32_t port)
 {
 	sg_port_t *sg_port;
+	void **slot;
    	sg_port = calloc(1,sizeof(sg_port_t));
     if(sg_port == NULL) {
 		L2MCD_LOG_ERR("%s alloc sg_port fail port:0x%x", FN, port);
@@ -2204,11 +2205,17 @@ int mld_sg_porttree_addport(L2MCD_AVL_TREE *port_tree, uint32_t port)
     }
 	M_AVLL_INIT_NODE(sg_port->node); 
     sg_port->ifindex = port;
-    if (!M_AVLL_INSERT(*port_tree,sg_port)){
+    slot = M_AVLL_INSERT(*port_tree,sg_port);
+    if (!slot){
 		L2MCD_LOG_NOTICE("%s insert sg_port to avl fail port:0x%x",FN, port);
        	free(sg_port);
        	return (-1);
     }
+    /* avl_probe() returns the port already in the tree, and leaves the new
+     * one out: a static port stays in the tree while its link is down, and
+     * its link-up replays the add (mld_static_grp_replay_confg()) */
+    if (*slot != sg_port)
+        free(sg_port);
     return 0;
 }
 
@@ -2522,7 +2529,15 @@ void mcgrp_refresh_l2_static_group(MCGRP_CLASS * mcgrp,
     {
 
         MCGRP_MBRSHP      *mcgrp_mbrshp = NULL;
+        MCGRP_PORT_ENTRY  *mcgrp_pport;
 		phy_port_id = sg_port->ifindex;
+        /* Only a port that is up is refreshed, as mcgrp_update_l2_static_group()
+         * makes the membership only for one: the timer keeps running while a
+         * port of the group is down (mcgrp_stop_phy_port()), and the port's
+         * static membership comes back with its link (mld_static_grp_replay_confg()). */
+        mcgrp_pport = mcgrp_find_phy_port_entry(mcgrp, mcgrp_vport, phy_port_id);
+        if (mcgrp_pport == NULL || !mcgrp_pport->is_up)
+            continue;
          // On update, the PIM/DVMRP functions get the port# from this data struct
         mcgrp_mbrshp = mcgrp_find_mbrshp_entry_for_grpaddr(mcgrp,
                                                            group_address,
diff --git a/src/igmp.c b/src/igmp.c
index b93ad6c..28fb554 100644
--- a/src/igmp.c
+++ b/src/igmp.c
@@ -622,7 +622,6 @@ void mcgrp_stop_phy_port (MCGRP_CLASS       *mcgrp,
 
     MCGRP_ENTRY         *mcgrp_entry, *next_entry;
     MCGRP_MBRSHP        *mcgrp_mbrshp;
-    MCGRP_STATIC_ENTRY  *mcgrp_static_entry;
     UINT16               vir_port_id = mcgrp_vport->vir_port_id;
     UINT32               phy_port_id = mcgrp_pport->phy_port_id;
     BOOLEAN              is_pim_snp_mbr;
@@ -648,17 +647,11 @@ void mcgrp_stop_phy_port (MCGRP_CLASS       *mcgrp,
         mcgrp_notify_phy_port_del(mcgrp, &mcgrp_entry->group_address,
                 mcgrp_vport, phy_port_id, TRUE);
 
-        //Stop wheeltimer on static group 
-        mcgrp_static_entry = mcgrp_find_l2_staticGroup(mcgrp, vir_port_id, &mcgrp_entry->group_address);
-        if (mcgrp_static_entry != NULL)
-        {
-             if (WheelTimerSuccess == WheelTimer_IsElementEnqueued
-                                        (&mcgrp_static_entry->l2_static_grp_tmr.mcgrp_wte))
-            {
-                WheelTimer_DelElement(mcgrp->mcgrp_wtid,  &mcgrp_static_entry->l2_static_grp_tmr.mcgrp_wte);
-                L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_DEBUG(vir_port_id, "%s:%d:[vlan:%d] Wheeltimer deleted from static Port:%d ", FN, LN, vir_port_id, phy_port_id);
-            }
-        }
+        // The static group's refresh timer is left running: it renews every
+        // port of the static group, not only this one, and stopping it here
+        // let the other ports' static memberships age out. The refresh skips
+        // a port that is not up (mcgrp_refresh_l2_static_group); this port's
+        // static membership comes back when it does (mld_static_grp_replay_confg).
 
         // Remove this port from the group membership. The membership is
         // freed by mcgrp_destroy_mbrshp_entry(), so what is needed of it is
